/** \file hciAnalyze_config.dox
 * \brief Configuration dictionary for hciAnalyze.
 * \author Jared R. Males
 */

/** \addtogroup hcianalyze_user_guide
 * @{
 *
 * \page hcianalyze_configuration_dictionary hciAnalyze configuration dictionary
 *
 * Long options use `--dotted.key value`; configuration files require a bare key under `[section]`, as described in
 * the shared configuration dictionary. The key/value columns use dotted shorthand only to keep the tables compact.
 *
 * \section hcianalyze_input Input and signal geometry
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `-f`, `--file` | `file=/path/product.fits` | readable FITS image or cube | required | PSF-subtracted product to analyze. |
 * | `--planet.sep` | `planet.sep=10,20` | nonnegative real-pixel vector | unset | Direct signal separations. Pair every value with `planet.PA`. |
 * | `--planet.PA` | `planet.PA=0,90` | finite degree vector | unset | Direct PAs east of north: north is up and east is left. |
 * | `--planet.R` | `planet.R=8` | one nonnegative real or one per signal | `10` | Signal exclusion radius or radii. |
 * | `--fake.sep` | `fake.sep=10,20` | nonnegative real-pixel vector | FITS keyword | Explicit fake separations; pair with `fake.PA`. |
 * | `--fake.PA` | `fake.PA=0,90` | finite degree vector | FITS keyword | Explicit fake PAs, east of north. |
 * | `--fake.contrast` | `fake.contrast=1e-4,1e-5` | one finite real per fake | FITS keyword | Fake contrasts included in output. |
 * | `--fake.R` | `fake.R=8` | one nonnegative real or one per fake | `10` | Fake exclusion radius or radii. |
 *
 * Do not mix explicit `planet` and `fake` settings. With neither group supplied, the FITS header must provide all of
 * `FAKESEP`, `FAKEPA`, and `FAKECONT`, encoded as comma-separated lists. Direct planets intentionally do not require
 * contrast metadata.
 *
 * \section hcianalyze_snr SNR and filtering
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--snr.minRad` | `snr.minRad=pixels` | finite real | `0` | Inner radial-noise bound. A non-positive value uses the minimum `REGMINR` or `HIERARCH P4 MIN RADIUS` header value. |
 * | `--snr.maxRad` | `snr.maxRad=pixels` | finite real | `0` | Outer radial-noise bound. A non-positive value uses the maximum `REGMAXR` or `HIERARCH P4 MAX RADIUS` header value. |
 * | `--snr.apertureR` | `snr.apertureR=pixels` | positive real | `2` | Radius of the aperture used to extract the reported `snr` value. |
 * | `--filter.hpfGaussFW` | `filter.hpfGaussFW=pixels` | finite real | `0` | High-pass Gaussian unsharp-mask FWHM; non-positive disables it. |
 * | `--filter.lpfGaussFW` | `filter.lpfGaussFW=pixels` | finite real | `0` | Low-pass Gaussian smoothing FWHM; non-positive disables it. |
 * | `--filter.perPixelPSF` | `filter.perPixelPSF=/path/p4PSF_manifest.fits` | complete P4 PSF manifest FITS path | unset | Apply the manifest's coordinate-indexed signed response field to the input cube before SNR calculation. This permits a response field measured from a signal-subtracted P4 reduction to filter the corresponding unsubtracted science product. |
 * | `-d`, `--diagnostics` | `diagnostics=true` | bool | `false` | Print resolved geometry, filters, invalid-pixel counts, and SNR values to standard error. |
 *
 * `filter.perPixelPSF` must name the `*_manifest.fits` file from a P4 run with `p4.outputPSFModels=true`.
 * hciAnalyze locates the sibling `coordinates`, `model_NNNN`, and `validity_NNNN` files from the manifest prefix. It
 * rejects incomplete sets and mismatched image planes, mode fractions, stamp geometry, coordinates, or product roles.
 * Filtering uses the recorded `P4 PSF FILTER MIN GOOD FRACTION` and the same signed normalized estimator as P4:
 * `sum(H*I)/sum(H*H)`. Pixels without a valid response remain excluded from the SNR calculation.
 *
 * Per-pixel PSF filtering runs first, followed by high-pass filtering and then low-pass smoothing when those Gaussian
 * filters are also enabled. At image edges and beside invalid input samples, the Gaussian filters use partial valid
 * in-bounds kernels and renormalize by their retained weights.
 * The reported `snr` is the aperture maximum inside `snr.apertureR`; `planet.R` or `fake.R` only excludes the signal
 * from the noise estimate.
 * hciAnalyze always writes or replaces the full SNR cube beside the input as `<input-stem>_snr<input-extension>`.
 * Its header records the resolved signal geometry, the resolved SNR annulus and aperture, both filter FWHMs, and the
 * per-pixel PSF manifest and minimum support when configured.
 *
 * @}
 */
